{"type":"message","id":"63e32fa2","parentId":"d2027a4f","timestamp":"2026-06-06T01:52:41.466Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The signature is `request(method, path, params=None)`. So `request(\"GET\", \"/fapi/v1/openAlgoOrders\", {})` should work (passing empty dict as params).\n\nAnd for DELETE: `request(\"DELETE\", \"/fapi/v1/algoOrder\", {\"algoId\": algo_id})` should also work.\n\nNow I also need to fix the dust position issue in the `need_rebuild` path. When the exchange has tiny amounts like 0.01, the code shouldn't reconstruct a full position from it. Let me also fix this.\n\nLet me also handle the minimum notional check. For DOT, the entry price is 0.954, so 0.01 * 0.954 * 10 (leverage) = 0.0954 USDT notional. That's well below the minimum.\n\nLet me check the minimum notional value on testnet. Usually it's $5.\n\nLet me add a dust filter:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now also fix the dust持仓导致反复重建的问题—— API 返回 0.01 这种粉尘仓位时，不应该重建为一个完整仓位："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_mkewGZ21PZJ5G1bbi58N5281","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '2337,2343p' /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":122,"output":508,"cacheRead":65408,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":66038,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780710754402}}
