{"type":"message","id":"a6dc2369","parentId":"746c08ff","timestamp":"2026-06-06T02:03:02.235Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so ETH is now flat but the 2 Algo orders remain. This is expected - we need the monitor's 5-minute sync to pick it up and clean it. Let me wait for the next sync and check the log.\n\nBut actually, the monitor was restarted at 08:17. The current time is around 10:03. Let me check when the next sync tick will happen. The sync is every 20 ticks (5 minutes), so the ticks are at: 08:17, 08:22, 08:27, etc. So the next sync should be at approximately 10:02 or 10:07.\n\nActually, let me just force a faster check by looking at the monitor log. Or we can wait.\n\nActually, let me just manually clean up the ETH orders now (since we proved the open+dispatch chain works) and focus on verifying the 5-minute sync with the DOT position (which was already opened by the monitor itself).\n\nWait - the DOT position was closed manually by us earlier. The monitor should have picked it up at the next 5-minute sync. Let me check the log.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_H4OMb2EIv2iVh8xN8tRa4295","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep \"持仓同步\\|清理\\|api_count\" /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log | tail -15"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":242,"output":541,"cacheRead":94336,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":95119,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780711372610}}
