{"type":"message","id":"2df03278","parentId":"59c3e6da","timestamp":"2026-06-06T05:27:13.769Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The scores are from 13:00. But it's now 13:26, so the data is 26 minutes old. Let me check if there's a more recent update. The hourly report runs every hour, and the signal updates are per-minute. Let me check the latest signal check.\n\nActually, the signal loop runs every ~60 seconds, but the \"评分详情\" is only logged at the hourly report. The per-tick scores might be in a different format. Let me check the most recent tick output.\n\nBut actually, the market is crashing and all coins are in deep oversold territory (RSI < 30 for all). The problem is the scoring formula heavily favors LONG when RSI is low. But the sentiment is bearish, so the MA60 filter (MA60:✗ for all) is blocking the signals.\n\nWait, looking at the scores:\n- ETH: 45分, RSI:4, -12.5% → MA60:✗ blocks it\n- SOL: 60分, RSI:12, -10.2% → MA60:✗ blocks it  \n- DOT: 60分, RSI:10, -12.3% → MA60:✗ blocks it\n- LINK: 60分, RSI:11, -10.4% → MA60:✗ blocks it\n\nThe MA60 filter is \"价格≥MA60 做多+20分，≤MA60 做空+20分\". Since all coins are below MA60, they get +20 for SHORT. But RSI is so low (<30) that it gives +35 for LONG. And the 24h change is heavily negative, giving +25 for LONG.\n\nSo the scores show:\n- SHORT: RSI +0 (not >65), 24h +0 (not up >5%), MA60 +20, vol +? = 20\n- LONG: RSI +35 (all <35), 24h +25 (all down >5%), MA60 +0, vol +? = 60\n\nThat's why the scores are mostly 60 for LONG (RSI +35, 24h +25) and crossing with the trading threshold.\n\nThe problem is: in this crash, going LONG is suicide. The MA60 filter correctly prevents LONG signals (MA60:✗ means price is below MA60, so the LONG signal gets 0 from MA60 component).\n\nBut this is the intended behavior - the scoring system is designed to NOT open LONG positions in a downtrend (MA60:✗), even when RSI is oversold. This prevents \"catching a falling knife.\"\n\nThe scores show 30-60 but the signal output is NONE for all - meaning the scoring threshold (70 for trending, 30 for ranging) isn't being met, or there's another filter blocking.\n\nWait, for a RANGING market, the threshold is ≥30. SOL, DOT, LINK all have 60, which is ≥30. But they show NONE. Let me think...\n\nThe signal output says NONE for all. The 60 score might be the LONG score, but the SHORT score might be lower. If the SHORT score doesn't reach the threshold, it outputs NONE.\n\nActually, let me re-read the scoring code:\n- Max score between long_score and short_score\n- For RSI: <35 → LONG +35, >65 → SHORT +35\n- For 24h: down >5% → LONG +25, up >5% → SHORT +25  \n- For MA60: above → LONG +20, below → SHORT +20\n- Volume: >avg → +20\n\nSo for SOL in a crash:\n- LONG: RSI(12) → +35, 24h(-10.2%) → +25, MA60:✗ → 0, vol → ? = 60\n- SHORT: RSI(12) → 0, 24h(-10.2%) → 0, MA60:✗ → +20, vol → ? = 20\n\nThe overall score selects the max (60), but the signal is output based on which direction wins. If LONG wins (60 vs 20), the signal output would be the LONG score (60). But it shows NONE because...\n\nOh wait, the output says \"信号：NONE\" for all. Let me check if the signal names are selected by long_score > short_score AND long_score >= threshold:\n\n```\nif long_score > short_score and long_score >= threshold:\n    return long_score, 'LONG'\nelif short_score > long_score and short_score >= threshold:\n    return short_score, 'SHORT'\n```\n\nFor SOL: LONG=60, SHORT=20, long_score > short_score ✓, long_score >= threshold (30 for ranging) ✓. So it should return (60, 'LONG').\n\nBut the output shows NONE for all... \n\nHmm, maybe the per-symbol bonus reduces the effective threshold, or there's another check. Or maybe the market regime is \"trending\" (down), which has a threshold of 70, and 60 < 70.\n\nLooking at the output: \"SOL: 60分 → 信号：NONE\". If regime is \"trending\" then threshold is 70, and 60 < 70 → NONE.\n\nThat makes sense! The market regime must be \"trending\" for all coins because the EMA slope is strongly negative, requiring a higher threshold.\n\nOK, this is fine - the system is working as intended. During a crash, the regime is \"trending\" which raises the threshold to 70, preventing counter-trend LONG entries even when RSI is extremely oversold.\n\nLet me just report the scores to 老公.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_INwJhKdt55k2YotqsQkZ7337","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep \"信号：\" /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log | tail -8"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":330,"output":2509,"cacheRead":77824,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":80663,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780723609279}}
